ective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name a concretely Windows-viable dual-pipe draining mechanism (e.g. per-pipe reader threads, or document that selectors-based reads are gated to POSIX with a stated Windows path) so the incremental reader does not crash on the supported Windows platform.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.801,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"Use non-blocking `selectors.DefaultSelector` registration for stdout and stderr\"","\"drains stdout and stderr incrementally with `selectors.DefaultSelector` or an equivalent dual-pipe nonblocking mechanism\"","Platform fact: Python's selectors/select on Windows only supports sockets, not OS pipe/file handles from subprocess.Popen"],"finding":"The plan's primary named mechanism, `selectors.DefaultSelector` registered on subprocess stdout/stderr pipes, is not portable to Windows: on Windows the default selector is select-based and cannot poll non-socket file handles (anonymous pipes), so registering the subprocess pipe fds raises an error. The plan hedges with 'or an equivalent dual-pipe nonblocking mechanism' but names no Windows-viable alternative.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f83d244a990f03705","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 1 / Context item 1","norm_id":"naa7daae2556da2ee","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Platform=Windows: the corroborator registers the terraform-config-inspect subprocess stdout/stderr pipes with selectors.DefaultSelector, select() rejects the non-socket handles, and the corroborator raises/crashes instead of grounding — every Terraform corroboration on Windows breaks"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the reader/reap handoff and deadline accounting: compute each select() timeout as remaining budget against DEADLINE_SECONDS, and on cap-exceeded stop reading and delegate to reap_process_group (relying on its SIGTERM->grace->SIGKILL->bounded-drain) rather than blocking on a full-pipe communicate().","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4763,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'drains stdout and stderr incrementally with selectors.DefaultSelector ... under the existing deadline'","Plan: 'Timeout and cap cleanup delegates process-group reaping to rebar._proc.reap_process_group'","Code: reap_process_group calls proc.communicate(timeout=grace) at _proc.py:89 and proc.communicate(timeout=drain) at :101 — draining pipes the selector reader may have already consumed to EOF","Code: current _run enforces a single wall-clock budget via proc.communicate(timeout=DEADLINE_SECONDS) (line 302); a naive per-select() timeout could reset that budget or block indefinitely on the cap-exceeded (child blocked on full pipe) path"],"finding":"The plan specifies switching to a selectors-based incremental drain AND delegating abort cleanup to reap_process_group, but does not address the interaction: reap_process_group internally calls proc.communicate() on the same pipes the new reader has already partially/fully drained, and the selector loop's per-iteration timeout must be budgeted against the single 60s DEADLINE_SECONDS (not reset each iteration) to preserve the existing total-deadline semantics.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f092e0432693ee159","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC lines 1-2 (selectors drain + reap delegation); src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py _run","norm_id":"nf4dc91af8c6bd8e7","priority":0.1237,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Cap exceeded mid-stream: reader stops, child blocked writing to a now-unread full pipe; reap must SIGTERM/SIGKILL before communicate() can drain remaining bytes","Selector loop uses a fixed per-iteration timeout, resetting the 60s budget each iteration and allowing total runtime to exceed the deadline"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_ratio